# Who gets a review request when a pull request touches a path.
#
# The list is the paths where a change is cheap to write and expensive to get
# wrong: what the build pulls in, what CI is allowed to do, and what a release
# ships. A plausible-looking edit to any of them can move the supply chain of
# every install without changing a line of Lumen's own code, so those files get
# a named reviewer rather than the general read-through the rest of the tree
# gets.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so the catch-all comes first.

*                       @FizzWizzleDazzle

# What the build resolves and from where. A dependency source or a pinned hash
# is the one kind of diff whose effect is entirely outside the diff.
/Cargo.toml             @FizzWizzleDazzle
/Cargo.lock             @FizzWizzleDazzle
**/Cargo.toml           @FizzWizzleDazzle
/rust-toolchain.toml    @FizzWizzleDazzle
/.cargo/                @FizzWizzleDazzle

# What CI runs, what it is permitted to do, and which actions it trusts.
/.github/               @FizzWizzleDazzle

# What a release builds, signs, and publishes, and what users download.
/tools/release/         @FizzWizzleDazzle
/tools/setup-lumen/     @FizzWizzleDazzle

# Licensing and contribution terms.
/LICENSE                @FizzWizzleDazzle
/CLA.md                 @FizzWizzleDazzle
/CONTRIBUTING.md        @FizzWizzleDazzle
/PHILOSOPHY.md          @FizzWizzleDazzle
